{"id":"DRKS00038147","src":"drks","title":"Quality Assurance in Ovarian Cancer 2025","official":"","summary":"The treatment of patients with ovarian cancer shall be recorded and analyzed with this study nationwide. Purpose is to examine the quality of treatment. Based on this recognition, conclusions for measures of an improvement of the treatment quality shall be drawn (e.g. improvement and adjustment of guidelines), that means systematically developed and scientific justified recommendations for an appropriate medically approach).\r\nAround 1000 female patients in 160 hospitals will participate in this study. The cohort includes patients, who are newly diagnosed with ovarian cancer in the 3rd quarter 2025.\r\nWithin this study exclusively data of the routine treatments shall be recorded and analyzed over a 5 years period. This are following data: current age, details of disease stage and results of histological examination  of the tumor tissue, so called prognostic marker, where applicable surgery details and systemic treatments with start and stop date (including if applicable maintenance treatments), and reason for early treatment termination if applicable. In addition all data of recurrence/progression, and if applicable, subsequent treatment steps.","conditions":["Malignant neoplasm of ovary"],"interventions":[{"type":"ARM","name":"The subject of this voluntary quality assurance measure is the nationwide collection of data on of the surgical steps and systemic treatments used (chemotherapies and targeted therapies) in clinical routine on patients who were newly diagnosed in the 3rd quarter of 2025. In addition, the relapse and"}],"criteria":"Inclusion criteria:\nInvasive epithelial ovarian cancer, fallopian tube, peritoneal cancer (including STIC lesions) or borderline tumours or rare ovarian malignancies including germ cell tumours and stromal cell tumours\nExclusion criteria:\nCancers of unknown primary\r\nBenign tumours of the ovary","minAge":"18 Years","ma